rfc8878-appendix-a.txt
    RFC 8878, "Zstandard Compression and the 'application/zstd' Media Type" (Y. Collet, M. Kucherawy,
    February 2021), Appendix A "Decoding Tables for Predefined Codes".
    Downloaded from https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8878.txt on 2026-10-25 (page breaks removed).
    License: IETF Trust Legal Provisions (code components and test vectors may be reproduced).
    Note: the first row of each table (state 0, all fields 0) precedes the real state 0 and is not a
    state of the table; the tests skip it.
*.zst, dictionary.trained
    Made on 2026-10-25 from the inputs of ../deflate and checked to decompress with the zstd tool:
    - with the zstd command line utility v1.5.7: text.level1, text.level3, repetitive.level19,
      random.level3, zeros.level3, empty (`zstd -1`, `-3`, `-19`), text.nocheck (`-3 --no-check`);
      large.level9, large.level22 (`--ultra -22`) and large.long (`-3 --long=27`) from an input of 284409
      bytes not stored here (the frames carry its XXH64, which the decoder checks, and its size);
      dictionary.trained (`zstd --train` on 2000-byte pieces of text.bin and repetitive.bin,
      `--maxdict=4096`), text.dictionary (`-3 -D dictionary.trained`), text.rawdictionary
      (`-3 -D ../deflate/dictionary.bin`, a raw content dictionary);
    - frames: text.level1 then random.level3; skippable: a skippable frame (magic 0x184D2A5E, 3 bytes
      "abc") then text.level3, made by hand;
    - text.streamed: Python 3.14 compression.zstd (libzstd 1.5.7) at level 5, fed in two pieces (a frame
      without its content size).
